A||||6||bwaits||Lets build a race car II||||1||
Z||000000||bwaits||05-24-2000||07:11 PM||||Thanks everyone for there help. I also posted this on a mailing list and had good <BR>responses there as well.<P>We have decided on the 88 formula. This will be a "project car" for a division of my <BR>company called SmartParts.  <A HREF="http://www.braits.com/smartparts" TARGET=_blank>http://www.braits.com/smartparts</A> <P>You can follow along with the construction, R&D through competition if you <BR>would like.<P>I noticed a post about the 88 cradle being solid mounted verses the bushings used on <BR>previous. My question is this, Does the cradle move while the suspension travels or <BR>is it fixed in location? There are rear control arms mounted to the cradle, correct?<P>Were there different manual transmissions from the 88 GT and the 88 Formula?<P>Anyone know of a place that might have a formula roller? We would consider just <BR>about any condition.||||reg||1
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||05-25-2000||12:06 AM||||Not sure what you mean by "I noticed a post about the 88 cradle being solid mounted verses the bushings used on <BR>previous. My question is this, Does the cradle move while the suspension travels or <BR>is it fixed in location?" but the cradle does not move at all. There are no "control arms" in the rear of 88s. They use trailing arms (they are bolted to the cradle) and lateral link and then the tie rods.<P>The 88 GT and Formula have the same manual tranny.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||05-25-2000||11:57 AM||||Formula and GT drivetrain and suspension are the same. Difference is in the body.<P>Also... 88 coupe (4 cyl) is the same as Formula EXCEPT: drivetrain (engine and tranny), spring rates, shocks?, and NO rear swaybar.<P><B>If</B> you are planning on using a different engine and suspension mods anyhow you could probably save some $$$ and have an easier time finding a coupe. Just a thought...<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||05-25-2000||02:06 PM||||Bwaits,<P>Where are you guys? <BR>By the area code, I can tell you're in the Atlanta area, someplace. <BR>BTW... There *should be* a meeting of the GA Fieros, this Saturday (unless they cancel it due to the holiday), at American Pie, on Roswell Rd. <BR>It's usually the last Saturday of every month. 1:30 PM. ||||reg||6
Z||000004||bwaits||05-25-2000||09:42 PM||||I finally got my fiero manual and answered my cradle question. Shouldn't have any <BR>more stupid questions.<P>We are unable to swap the 4 cylinder for the 6 cylinder using the coupe. It has to be <BR>the make model and engine listed. <P>We are in Lawrenceville. 30 miles north of Atlanta. How can I get in touch to see <BR>when they meet. I will be in South Carolina this weekend for an endurance race.<P>-billy<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B>Bwaits,<P>Where are you guys? <BR>By the area code, I can tell you're in the Atlanta area, someplace. <BR>BTW... There *should be* a meeting of the GA Fieros, this Saturday (unless they cancel it due to the holiday), at American Pie, on Roswell Rd. <BR>It's usually the last Saturday of every month. 1:30 PM. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
